From: WL2GO
Subject: Bind the WebGui listener too, and remove the dev-mode host-command path

Two changes, both closing the gap patch 0005 recorded as KNOWN GAP.

1. ws_server binds its listener independently of --hostbind, through its own
   getaddrinfo(NULL, port, AI_PASSIVE) -- the textbook "listen on everything"
   form. So the command and data ports could sit on loopback while the WebGui
   port did not. ws_set_bind_addr() follows the existing ws_set_port() shape,
   and Webgui.c hands it the same HostBindAddr the host interface uses.

   The upstream default is preserved: with no --hostbind, behaviour is
   unchanged.

2. The "developer mode" reached by passing a NEGATIVE --webgui port is removed
   from this build. It is the only gate on the Webgui 'H' message, which feeds
   arbitrary text to ProcessCommandFromHost() -- including RADIOPTTON. A bind
   address is the right fix for reachability, but it is one mistyped argument
   away from being wrong, and a remote transmitter-keying path should not
   depend on nobody ever passing that argument. Upstream itself describes the
   feature as "an 'undocumented' feature that may be discontinued in future
   releases".

   A negative port is now a hard exit with a reason rather than a mode switch,
   so the 'H' path is unreachable in the binary WL2GO ships.

NOTE what neither change covers: the Webgui '2' message fires TWOTONETEST -- a
real five-second transmission -- and is NOT gated by dev mode. That is why the
bind address in (1) is not optional, and it is a constraint on any tuning UI
later built over this interface.

